{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
  "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: ALAN UNTEREINER, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners. LISA S. BLATT, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, if we were to agree with you on any one of the three questions, would that end the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our second argument is that the Hobbs Act does not punish freestanding acts or threats of violence. By \"freestanding,\" we mean unconnected to either robbery or extortion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is the position of the United States that the physical-violence clause of the Hobbs Act requires an intended robbery or extortion, and that private parties, under RICO, cannot obtain injunctive relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I identify a concern? I'd like you to help me out on it. I -- that language, if you construe it the way the other side does, it would cover certain violent conspiracies that would merely obstruct interstate commerce that we could all be concerned about today."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The FACE Act, which was passed in 1994, gives private parties a right for damages and injunctive relief for blocking access to clinics."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CHEMERINSKY",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Seventh Circuit did exactly the right thing in this case. It sent the case back to the District Court and asked the District Court to determine whether an injunction could remain, based on the four counts of physical violence and threats of violence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, you say \"most favorable to its conclusion,\" but did the jury conclude that there should be an injunction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, since this is an injunction, he is allowed to consider the evidence that he heard, since he was sitting in an equitable matter. And so, there were actually two presentations --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the Seventh Circuit in its most recent expression said, \"It may well be that the judge will decide that those 4 predicate acts\" -- as opposed to 121 going in, 4 -- \"were not sufficient to support certainly a nationwide injunction, but perhaps not any injunction.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there anything that -- under your reading of the Hobbs Act, that isn't covered by the FACE Act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't -- I don't understand your argument on that point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is simple. We believe that the Hobbs Act was changed precisely to deal with the situations where there might be a radical animal-activist group that might be blowing up restaurants that serve meat, or clothing stores, or where there might be situations where racists were blowing up businesses owned by blacks or Jews. That's what the Hobbs Act does."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the RICO statute provides, as Congress intended, a broad remedial scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Your Honor, that would then assume that this Court decided an issue about the meaning of the Hobbs Act that was never presented in the cert petitions, never briefed, never addressed in the opinion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Untereiner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fd5eeabc9fd68a299b0472553863f32138246c9eb01ea330c6c2187f522848db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fd5eeabc9fd6-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I just would like to point out that the Hobbs Act also covers official extortion, which does not require acts or threats of violence."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
